		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T22:55:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Ensure extension manifest fields and type filtering work correctly\n\nFour related fixes address extension loading failures and missing activation:\n\n1. Manifest field serialization: Remove `skip_serializing_if` from Name, Version, Publisher fields. VS Code's trusted-publishers migration calls `manifest.publisher.toLowerCase()` at boot—if the key is omitted, the renderer crashes with `TypeError: undefined is not an object`. Add IPC handler hardening with explicit fallback values.\n\n2. Extension type filtering: Respect the ExtensionType filter passed to `getInstalled(type?)`. Previously all calls returned the full list as `type: 0, isBuiltin: true`. Now System extensions (type=0) and User extensions (type=1, including VSIX) are properly distinguished. Forward filters from `scanSystemExtensions` and `scanUserExtensions` handlers.\n\n3. Post-install activation: Fire `onStartupFinished` activation events after `$deltaExtensions` adds an extension. Without this, extensions like `Anthropic.claude-code` register but never activate—sidebar contributions silently no-op until restart.\n\n4. Log file eager init: Call `InitEager()` at binary startup to preserve logs before any panic. Fix `BinarySignature()` PascalCase splitting. Expand benign ENOENT ignore list.\n\nImpact: VSIX extensions now show under \"Installed\" with Uninstall, activate immediately after install without reload, and the Extensions sidebar refresh works correctly.",
			"SHA": "dd606e20bdc57b03917454d8b6a2fc9cc4563fc7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T22:18:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Add shutdown guard and fix static asset path resolution\n\nAdd atomic shutdown guard to Entry.rs to prevent the graceful shutdown sequence from running twice. The graceful path ends with `app_handle.exit(0)` which Tauri re-delivers as a second `ExitRequested { code: Some(0) }`. On re-entry we must NOT `prevent_exit` or spawn the shutdown task again — Cocoon has already been SIGKILLed and the second pass would log spurious \"tcp connect error\" warnings.\n\nExtend static asset path resolution in Utilities.rs to handle both `/Static/Application/` and `Static/Application/` forms. The webview's WASM loader resolves asset URLs relative to the current document, which strips the leading slash before reaching the `file:read` IPC handler. Without this fix, `tokio::fs::read` would fail with ENOENT, breaking TextMate syntax highlighting.\n\nAlso expand the benign ENOENT ignore list in DevLog.rs to suppress warnings for `.copilot/agents`, `.vscode/tasks.json`, `/User/tasks.json`, `/User/mcp.json`, `vscode-chat-images`, and `/output_<TIMESTAMP>` window log file patterns.\n\nThis prevents spurious shutdown warnings, fixes TextMate grammar loading, and reduces log noise.",
			"SHA": "bd38c344b6e75841edd53fa141b61eb9cb6a257b"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T20:26:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 2 components\n\nSynchronize Mountain and Sky submodules with the following changes:\n- **Mountain:** Simplify binary naming from verbose development profile identifier to just 'Mountain'. Update Tauri identifier to 'land.editor.binary'. Remove externalBin reference to Binary/node since Node.js sidecar is now handled differently. Add vscode-file and vscode-file://vscode-app to img-src Content Security Policy for VS Code file protocol support. Delete temporary backup files (Cargo.toml.Backup, tauri.conf.json.Backup).\n- **Sky:** Add exception signature throttling to PostHog bridge — exceptions share the `$exception` event-name slot in posthog-js, so a burst of CSP refusals/console.error/unhandledrejection callbacks during workbench boot would blow through the 10/10s rate limit. Add a secondary throttle layer keyed by the first 200 chars of the error message. Both regular and exception drop counts are now reported in the `land:sky:throttle-dropped` event for visibility.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers build configuration simplification and PostHog rate limit protection while maintaining identical runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "ddf6e4aed3c5d003a92613262637479678a4a5f7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T19:45:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				100,
				1
			],
			"Message": "build(Project): Coordinate Element submodule updates across 7 components\n\nSynchronize Air, Cocoon, Grove, Mist, Mountain, Output, and Rest submodules with the following changes:\n- **Air:** Migrate SHA256 checksum generation to hex::encode for sha2 0.11 compatibility — sha2 crate 0.11 changed `Digest::finalize()` output from `GenericArray` to `hybrid_array::Array`. Replace format!(\"{:x}\", …) with hex::encode() across Daemon/Manager, Indexing/Scan/ScanFile, Indexing/State/CreateState, Security/ChecksumVerifier, Updates/UpdateManager, and Vine/Server/AirVinegRPCService.\n- **Mist:** Update to hickory-server 0.26 API — Migrate from hickory-server 0.25 module reorganization (authority::* → zone_handler::*, InMemoryAuthority → InMemoryZoneHandler<T>, ServerFuture → Server, AXFR bool → AxfrPolicy enum). Add DNS_TCP_RESPONSE_BUFFER_SIZE constant (65,535 bytes) for TCP listener registration.\n- **Mountain:** Update build configuration for development profile — Rename binary, lib, and product to include DevelopmentNodeEnvironment_MicrosoftVSCodeDependency_22NodeVersion_Bundle_Clean_Debug_ElectronProfile_Mountain. Add Binary/node to externalBin in tauri.conf.json. Replace deprecated posthog-rs api_endpoint() with host(). Apply sha2 0.11 hex::encode migration to ConfigurationBridge.rs.\n- **Rest:** Migrate to OXC 0.127 API for codegen and transform — Replace flat `comments: bool` in CodegenOptions with structured CommentOptions type. Migrate from deprecated `into_symbol_table_and_scope_tree()` / `build_with_symbols_and_scopes()` to unified `into_scoping()` / `build_with_scoping()` returning a single Scoping value.\n\nThis coordinated update delivers dependency compatibility, API migrations, and build configuration alignment while maintaining identical runtime behavior.",
			"SHA": "3e906ccc0a626ad9cfe776034eaaefec78279f2c"
		}
	],
